  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015) is set up for his contrast CT on Monday 10/26 at 9:00. Everything below follows RBC-RAD-07.\n\n- **CT order:** CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast, pancreatic protocol (sr-t0001), linked to his 10/26 9:00 appointment.\n- **Contrast reaction grade:** moderate, so he needs premedication, not the no-contrast rule for severe reactions. The radiology report from the day of his 2019 iohexol reaction calls it moderate: hives and mild eyelid swelling, with no breathing or airway problems. His allergy list also says \"anaphylaxis,\" but that was added in 2021 from his own account without checking records. The policy grades by the record of the day, so it doesn't change the grade. I left the allergy entry as it is. His shellfish and povidone-iodine allergies are not risk factors.\n- **Premedication:** prednisone 50 mg by mouth on Sunday 10/25 at 20:00, then Monday 10/26 at 02:00 and 08:00 (mr-t0003). Diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth Monday at 08:00 (mr-t0004). He must not drive after the diphenhydramine and needs a driver.\n- **Kidney test before the scan:** he needs a creatinine within 30 days of the scan because he is 64 and diabetic. His 9/24 value of 1.02 falls outside that window. His ED values from 10/16–17 (1.94, then 1.46 at discharge) were drawn during an acute kidney injury after gastroenteritis, so they don't count. I ordered a creatinine ASAP, to be drawn before Monday 08:30 (sr-t0002). The scan stays as booked, and the radiologist will review the result that day.\n- **Metformin:** because of the recent kidney injury, I put metformin 1000 mg twice daily on hold now, through the scan and for at least 48 hours after. I ordered a repeat creatinine for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006). I also made a follow-up task for you, due 10/30 (task-t0007), to restart metformin only if his kidney function is normal.\n- **Patient instructions:** I sent him an ASAP portal message (comm-t0008). It covers the blood test, the medicine times, the driver requirement and stopping metformin until we call him. It also covers fluids, blood sugar checks while he's off metformin, and the signs of a reaction to watch for.\n- **Chart note:** documentation is in doc-t0009.\n\nSince the instructions went by portal message only, it may be worth calling him to make sure he sees them before Sunday evening.",
